  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced partnerships and improved multilateral cooperation to promote integrated policy responses for social justice through decent work in Brazil.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO is implemented by the South-South Cooperation and Strategic Partnerships Area of the ILO Office for Brazil, the only ILO field office with a dedicated structure for South-South Cooperation (SSC). 
SSC has become a strategic priority in Brazil&#x2019;s foreign policy and a key pillar of its partnership with the ILO. Since its formalization in 2009, the Brazil-ILO Programme has promoted the Decent Work Agenda through knowledge-sharing and mutual learning, particularly in areas such as child and forced labour, social protection, and green jobs across Latin America, Africa, and Asia.
This partnership has evolved further under the 2023&#x2013;2027 programme, &#x201c;Social Justice for the Global South,&#x201d; which focuses on strengthening capacities in priority areas including labour rights, occupational safety and health, equality, and social protection. Within this framework, the CPO aims to promote social dialogue, inclusion, and decent work for youth. Key activities include supporting national social dialogue processes, facilitating international knowledge exchange, strengthening capacities on FPRW and International Labour Standards, and advancing youth employment and leadership initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
